@startuml
title One exporter cache owner; clear cannot be undone by old work
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
actor "Foreign caller / resource clone" as Caller #DCEDC8
participant "lling-llang exporter" as Exporter #FCF3CF
participant "Shared state cache" as Cache #BBDEFB
database "Atomic root\nresidents + exact LRU order" as Root #C8E6C9
participant "Duallity direct source" as Source #D6EAF8
participant "Captured dictionary revision" as Dictionary #D5F5E3
actor "Native cache control" as Control #FFECB3

Caller -> Exporter: state_info or state_arcs(id)
Exporter -> Cache: lookup(id)
Cache -> Root: read immutable root
Root --> Cache: miss; generation G
note over Cache #BBDEFB: Drop the root guard; retain only the small G marker.
Cache -> Source: compute once
Source -> Dictionary: checked snapshot traversal
Control -> Cache: clear()
Cache -> Root: atomically replace with empty generation H
Dictionary --> Source: complete expansion or provider fault
Source --> Cache: checked result
alt invalid or failed
  Cache --> Exporter: original invalid result / error; no admission
else valid successful result
  Cache -> Root: read current generation
  Root --> Cache: H differs from G
  Cache --> Exporter: return old request's value; do not populate H
end
Exporter --> Caller: finality / requested arc page / error
note over Caller,Root #ECEFF1
New requests may populate H. Eviction never resets state identifiers.
CacheAll and already-MRU hits need no root update.
Other LRU hits publish link changes while sharing payload ownership.
end note
@enduml
